{{also|allah|Alláh|Allâh}}
==English==
{{wp}}
{{wikiquote}}

===Alternative forms===
*{{alt|en|Alha||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ar|ء ل ه}}
From {{der|en|ar|اللّٰه}}, contraction of {{m|ar|اَل||the}} + {{m|ar|إِلَه||deity}}; cognate with the {{cog|arc|אלה|tr=aláh}} and {{m|arc|אלהא|tr=aláhâ}}, and {{cog|he|אֵל|tr=él}}, {{m|he|אלוה|אֱלוֹהַּ / אֱלֹהַּ|tr=elóah}} and {{m|he|אלוהים|אֱלוֹהִים \ אֱלֹהִים|tr=elohím}}; ultimately from {{der|en|sem-pro|*ʾil-}}.-.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈlɑː/}}, {{IPAchar|/ˈɑːlɑː/}},<ref name="MW">{{R:Merriam Webster Online}}</ref> {{IPAchar|/ˌɑːˈlɑː/}}<ref name="MW"/> {{qualifier|pronunciation which is close to the standard Arabic pronunciation {{IPAchar|[ʔalˤˈlˤɑːh]}}}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæ.lə/}},<ref name="dictcom">{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><ref name="MW"/> {{IPAchar|/ˈɑːlə/}}<ref name="dictcom"/><ref name="MW"/> {{qualifier|anglicized pronunciations; close to dialectal Arabic {{IPAchar|[ˈʔɑlˤlˤa]}}}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Allah.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː|ælə|s=2}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2095353}}{{lb|en|Islam}} [[God]], in [[Islam]]ic or Arabic contexts
#: {{ux|en|What is the Shia Islamic view on the attributes of '''Allah'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=w:Anne Rice|title=The Vampire Armand|location=New York|publisher=Knopf
|isbn=9780679454472|ol=354828M|page=273
|passage=We are too much men and women; we are yet formed in the image of the Creator, and what can we say of Him with any certainty except that He, whoever He may be—Christ, Yahweh, '''Allah'''—He made us, did He not, because even He in His Infinite Perfection could not bear to be alone.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|work=w:Truth Social|author=w:Donald Trump<alt:Donald John Trump>|url=https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/116351998782539414|date=5.4.2026|text=[[Tuesday]] [[will]] [[be]] [[power plant|Power Plant]] [[Day]], [[and]] [[bridge|Bridge]] [[Day]], [[all]] [[wrapped]] [[up]] [[in]] [[one]], [[in]] [[Iran]]. [[there|There]] [[will]] [[be]] [[nothing]] [[like]] [[it]]!!! [[open|Open]] [[the]] [[fuckin'|Fuckin’]] [[strait|Strait]], [[you]] [[crazy]] [[bastards]], [[or]] [[you]][[-'ll|’ll]] [[be]] [[living]] [[in]] [[Hell]] - [[just|JUST]] [[watch|WATCH]]! [[praise be|Praise be]] [[to]] '''Allah'''. [[President]] [[Donald|DONALD]] [[J.]] [[Trump|TRUMP]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261011050048/https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/116351998782539414|archivedate=11 October 2026}}

====Usage notes====
While in Arabic {{l|ar|اللّٰه}} is used generically to refer to God in Jewish, Christian, and Islamic contexts, current English usage almost always restricts the corresponding English term {{m|en||Allah}} to Islamic contexts only. Various newspaper style manuals recommend translating the Arabic word in English as ''God'', as this better reflects Arabic usage, but the term is often left untranslated in Islamic contexts. Thus either “Allah is great” or “God is great” may be seen.

