====Usage notes====
* In Islamic contexts, this word may alternatively be translated into English as [[Allah]]. Note, however, that the Arabic word is just as neutral and general as English [[God]], and does not express any particularly Islamic notion at all. {{m|ar|اللَّٰه}} is the Arabic word used by Christians, Jews, and other monotheists to describe the God of their own religions, and is cognate to the words used in Hebrew and Syriac. The Jewish sage {{w|Saadia Gaon}} even used {{m|ar|اللَّٰه}} to translate the {{w|Tetragrammaton}} in his Arabic translation of the Torah.

